# u32_codepoint_index.tkr — the SM-STRU32 codec fixture. `main.tks` calls
# `teko::text::str_to_u32(s)` on an ASCII string and checks every index: the codepoint view has
# the same length as the string's bytes, and each `u32` codepoint equals the byte at that index
# (ASCII bytes are their own codepoint). Exits 0 only if every index matches.

Feature: u32_codepoint_index — str_to_u32 gives an O(1)-indexable codepoint view

  Scenario: str_to_u32_codepoints_match_ascii_bytes_by_index
    When the program is built and run
    Then it exits 0
